    say where the file comes from.

The function plant_gate in verify.py implements the predicate of Weft interface I3. It was written from
Weft's interface note, its conformance vectors and its reference implementation, and its arithmetic
follows the reference so that the two agree exactly. No Weft code is imported or copied into it. The
vendored invariants.py is run only as the oracle of a differential test.

The other files under data/upstream/ are certificates from aska-physical repositories
(funi-frame, funi-floors, venturi-collars), copied unmodified. data/upstream/MANIFEST.json records the
source commit and SHA-256 of each file.

Short quotations from other repositories appear in data/pins.json, data/graph.json and the documents as
the text of citations. Each names its repository, commit, file and line.

